  "faq9Q": "Why does the app ask for permissions?",
  "faq9A": "On Android: \"Run in background\" so the counter is not killed by battery optimisation, and \"Notifications\" because Android requires a visible notification for background services. On iPhone both permissions are optional: \"Focus\" to give a bonus for Do Not Disturb, and \"Screen Time\" to verify that the phone was not used during a session. Everything is read on the phone and never shared. You can change your mind under More → Permissions.",
  "faq10Q": "Does it use a lot of battery?",
  "faq10A": "No. The counter only listens for system events (screen, sound profile, airplane mode) and uses the phone's low-power motion sensor. It does not measure continuously.",
  "faq11Q": "What is the plan going forward?",
  "faq11A": "Groups and challenges (\"no screen before 9\"), streaks, a home screen widget, and a web version of the standings. Suggestions are welcome.",
  "faq12Q": "Who is behind it, and how do I get in touch?",
  "faq12A": "Free Time is a small, independent project with no ads and no selling of data. Write to {email} with questions, bugs or ideas.",
